thern cuisine|Southern cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Holiday Recipes|Holiday Recipes]]\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (⅓ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]]/85 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Cream Cheese|cream cheese]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire Sauce]]\n* ¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] ({{convert|25|g|oz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Green Onion|green onions]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Green Pepper|green peppers]]\n* [[Cookbook:Chop|Chopped]] [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushroom]] stems\n* 2 slices cooked [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]], chopped\n* ½ cup ({{convert|40|g|oz|abbr=on|disp=s}}) [[Cookbook:Bread Crumbs|bread crumbs]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 2 dozen [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|325°F]] (about 160–165°C).\n# Soften cream cheese and put in [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]]. Add Worcestershire sauce, salt, and pepper; pulse until mixed.\n# [[Cookbook:Folding|Fold]] in chopped bacon, chopped mushroom stems, diced green onions, and green peppers.\n# Set stuffing aside.\n# Mix bread crumbs with just enough butter to hold together.\n# Stuff mushroom caps with stuffing.\n# Top with bread crumbs.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for 5 minutes.\n\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream cheese]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mushroom]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stuffing and dressing]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mushroom Caps Stuffed with Bacon and Cheese","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingre